== Post-match ==

=== Reaction ===
[[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] reclaimed the [[EFL Cup]] for the first time in five years since their 1–0 triumph in the [[2021 EFL Cup final|2021 final]] against [[Ryan Mason]]'s [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]]. On the other hand, this denied [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] their first major trophy in six years since the [[2020 FA Cup final|2020 final]] against [[Arsenal F.C.–Chelsea F.C. rivalry|North-West London derby]] rivals [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] in a 2–1 triumph.<ref>{{Cite web |last=EFL |date=2026-03-22 |title=Reaction: Manchester City win the Carabao Cup |url=https://efl.com/news/2026/march/22/live--carabao-cup-final-arsenal-v-manchester-city/ |access-date=2026-03-23 |website=EFL |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil |title=Carabao Cup final: Nico O'Reilly double helps Man City beat Arsenal at Wembley |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/live/cy030p56zx4t |access-date=2026-03-23 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mumford |first=Jack |title=Guardiola sets record for most League Cup wins as a manager |url=https://www.mancity.com/news/mens/Guardiola%20sets%20record%20for%20most%20League%20Cup%20wins%20as%20a%20manager |access-date=2026-03-23 |website=Manchester City FC |language=en}}</ref>

[[File:Pep Guardiola 2021.jpg|thumb|[[Pep Guardiola]] (''pictured in 2021'') won his fifth [[EFL Cup]] title which is the most of any manager in [[EFL Cup]] history beating the likes of [[José Mourinho]], [[Brian Clough]] and [[Alex Ferguson|Sir Alex Ferguson]] (who all have won four [[EFL Cup|EFL Cups]]) and [[Bob Paisley]] and [[George Graham]] (who have both won three [[EFL Cup|EFL Cups]])]]

==Broadcasting==
The final was televised live in the [[United Kingdom]] via pay-TV broadcaster [[Sky UK|Sky]], who showed the game on [[Sky One]], as well as the Sky Sports Main Event and Sky Sports Football channels. For the second year in a row, the Sky Sports Football channel was also simulcast on free-to-air channel [[ITV1]] ([[STV (TV channel)|STV]] in [[Scotland]]). The final was available for streaming on [[Sky Go]] and [[Now (streaming service)|Now]], with Sky's coverage also streamed live on [[ITVX]] and [[STV Player]].<ref>https://www.efl.com/news/2026/march/20/how-to-watch-the-carabao-cup-final-2026-on-tv/</ref> On radio, match coverage was aired on [[BBC Radio 5 Live]] and [[Talksport]]. It was also aired live on broadcast television through [[CBS]] and streamed on [[Paramount+]] in the [[United States]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-03-22 |title=Arsenal vs. Manchester City live stream: How to watch EFL Cup final, odds, start time |url=https://www.cbssports.com/soccer/news/manchester-city-efl-cup-arsenal-gunners-premier-league-live-stream/ |access-date=2026-04-04 |website=CBS Sports |language=en}}</ref>

